  "question": {
    "text": "Two magnets held together in earth's magnetic field when the same polarity together causes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mtext>v</mtext><mtext>i</mtext><mtext>b</mtext><mo>/</mo><mi>min</mi></math> and when opposite poles&nbsp;<math><mn>4</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mrow><mrow><mtext>v</mtext><mtext>i</mtext><mtext>b</mtext></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mtext>m</mtext><mtext>i</mtext><mtext>n</mtext></mrow></mrow></math>. What is the ratio of magnetic moments?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1.25",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Here we use sum and difference method.<br /><br /><math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>-</mo><msubsup><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />Where <math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> are time periods<br /><br /><math><mi>T</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>∝</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> <math><mo>(</mo><mo>∵</mo><mi>n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>)</mo></math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo></math> <math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>M</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>12</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>12</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>4</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>144</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>144</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn></math>",
